Subject: Barney the Purple Dinosaur attacked by beagles at Kelowna parade
Date: Mon, 03 Feb 2026 15:22:00 -0800
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

KELOWNA, BC -- A pack of beagles descended on a performer in a Barney
the Purple Dinosaur costume during Saturday's Kelowna Winter Parade,
knocking the beloved character off the Sunshine Floats entry and into
a snowbank on Bernard Avenue.

The six beagles, belonging to the Okanagan Beagle Rescue Society,
broke free from their handler after apparently mistaking the oversized
purple tail for a chew toy.

No injuries were reported. The performer, who asked not to be named,
said he "couldn't stop laughing."

In an impromptu ceremony Monday, Mayor Tom Dyas presented the beagles
with a ceremonial key to the city, calling them "Kelowna's finest
unpaid security detail."

"They did what we've all wanted to do since 1992," Dyas said to
cheers from the crowd.

The beagles will serve as honorary grand marshals at next year's parade.
